  "worked_solution": "We know that $g\u22a5h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-6)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}-{r}^{2}-12 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\sqrt{6}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
